[h1]Speculative Markets - Beta[/h1]
The testing channel for Speculative Markets, a Victoria 3 mod about investment, booms, financial panics, and the policies used to manage them.

[b]Enable either this Beta or the stable mod, never both.[/b] Beta is a complete mod, not an add-on. Disable stable manually before enabling Beta.

Changes are tested here before promotion to stable. Use a separate playset and keep copies of saves when trying experimental revisions.

[h2]Latest update[/h2]
[b]1.0.5-beta.1[/b]
Stable and beta currently have the same gameplay files.
[list]
[*]Fixed tied Exchange results, stale bank tooltips and overstated confidence losses at zero.
[*]Fixed missing confidence penalties after surrendering.
[*]Removed the Open Finance button from individual goods views. Use the sidebar or Financial Markets journal entry.
[/list]

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3831434383]Prefer the regular release? Use Speculative Markets here.[/url]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Using CMF? Add the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839275348]CMF patch[/url] and load it last.
[*]Using Morgenroete? Add the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3839705018]Morgenroete patch[/url]. Disable the old Speculative Markets+Morgenroete patch.
[/list]
With both, use this order: [b]CMF > Morgenroete > Speculative Markets > Morgenroete patch > CMF patch.[/b] You can use Beta in place of Speculative Markets. Don't enable both.

[h2]Reporting problems[/h2]
Include the beta version, game version, relevant mods and load order, and the steps that reproduce the problem. For Finance shortcuts, say which panel you opened from and which tab appeared. A screenshot or save from before the issue can help reproduce it.

Built against Victoria 3 1.15.1. This is the separate testing distribution of Speculative Markets; it is not Community Mod Framework itself.
